# Store every text file with LF, and check it out with LF on every platform.
#
# Several release gates hash or byte-compare tracked text files:
#   * scripts/release-manifest.cjs records the size and SHA-256 of EULA.md and
#     docs/partner-center-submission.md in dist/release-manifest.json;
#   * scripts/certification-audit.cjs byte-compares the sample report's embedded
#     visual resource against the resource in the freshly packaged .pbiviz.
#
# Git stores LF, so without eol=lf a Windows checkout writes CRLF and those
# hashes and comparisons silently disagree with the Linux CI runner - a failure
# that reproduces only in CI. eol=lf pins the working tree to match the index.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.pbiviz binary
*.pbix binary
